# replay-player

Vite + vanilla TypeScript. Debug viewer for GNU Backgammon SGF dumps ([ADR 0010](docs/decisions/0010-replay-player.md)).

- Input is `FF[4]` `GM[6]` match files from `move-dumper/dumps/<batch>/replay/` or `battle-arena/replays/`. File picker only. No JSONL, no backend, no React.
- From `replay-player/`: `npm run up` (http://localhost:5173), `npm test`, `npm run install:host`. Those wrap Compose; do not run `test:inner` / `dev` on the host.
- Previous / Next is one checker step or cube action.
- Reconstruct position JSON by applying checker steps and cube double / take / drop from the standard opening ([board-representation.md](docs/domain/board-representation.md)). Hits implied. Board helpers come from `ts-core`.
- Do not import `move-dumper`. Do not import `ts-core/match` (Node-only). Do not treat SGF as a training representation.
